mend uh to to eat for  like a good dinner a good lunch a good  breakfast that's great questions um yeah  so i think that just focusing on what  you can add rather than what you can  take away because when we have that  restrictive type of mentality it is what  gets us into this vicious diet cycle  where we're like okay well now i'm gonna  be on and then i'm going to be off and  it's like that all or nothing mentality  so really thinking about okay how can i  add protein that could be chicken that  could be eggs that could be fish how can  i eat fat avocados olives nuts seeds  fiber leafy greens green vegetables and  then a healthy carbs sweet potatoes  carrots squash those types of things and  i know you're really good about sharing  with your followers some sample diets  and if people want to see some of those  where can they find that they can find  that with me on my instagram first and  foremost wellnessbykelly.com  signing up for my newsletter we share  stuff like that all of the time you can  just do that on our website  and then in my app we share recipes  every single week such great info before  i let you go though i do want to ask  about the blood sugar and the mood yeah  and how the blood sugar affects our mood  so when you have that spike and crash  like we were talking about when you eat  like let's say oatmeal a banana or  someone who's going to eat a lot of  sugar or whatever maybe like pizza and  pasta just empty carbs that don't have  the protein fat and fiber to slow  everything down you're going to feel  more anxious you're going to feel less  focused you're going to feel more  fatigued throughout the day and you're  also  going to have the tendency to  potentially feel more depressed oh to  see this is so important everything  great great info thank you kelly thank  you again to wellness by kelly go check  her out for sponsoring the segment visit  wellness by  kelly.com kendall i
 

